// Generates all possible unique variants
// using depth-first search algorithm (dfs)
// and returns them as a slice of serialized keys.
// nolint:gocyclo

// isSelectedNow: when we backtrack, we must only undo selections introduced
			// by this level. If an outer recursion level had already selected this code,
			// we must leave it intact — otherwise we’d accidentally erase state that
			// another branch of the search still depends on.

// isInvalidDueToPreviousOccurrence
// If the candidate code appeared in a previous ExactlyOne group
// (i.e., it exists in previousPossibleChoices) but was not selected
// (i.e., it is not present in selected), then it is invalid to introduce it now.
//
// Example:
//   - Group 0: {opt1, opt2} → we selected opt2
//   - Group 1: {opt1, opt3} → we must not select opt1 here, because it
//     appeared earlier but was not chosen.

// isConflictWithExistingSelection
// If any other code in the same ExactlyOne group has already been selected
// (i.e., it exists in the selected map) and it is different from the current
// candidate (v) we are trying to choose, the function returns true.
// This ensures that once a component has been "locked" to a specific code,
// we cannot choose a different code for the same component in a later step.
//
// Example:
//   - Group 0: {opt1, opt2} → we selected opt1
//   - Group 1: {opt1, opt3} → we must not select opt3 here,
//     because the component is already locked to opt1.

