// Adjust for the edge case where January overlaps with the last week of the previous year.
	// Example: 2021-01-01 is in week 53 and is shared with 2020.
	// so ISOWeek returns week 53, (year 2020) for 2021-01-01.

// Adjust for the edge case where December overlaps to week 1.
	// Example: 2019-12-31 is in week 1 and is shared with 2020.
	// so ISOWeek returns week 1, (year 2020) for 2019-12-31.

// isBefore returns true if the receiver period is before the other period.
// If the "from" weeks are equal, the "to" weeks are compared such that the period
// that ends earlier is considered before.

// Subtract one week from the "from" of the other period to avoid overlap.
		// Example: If s is 2021-W01 to 2021-W10 and other is 2021-W05 to 2021-W10.
		// The difference should be 2021-W01 to 2021-W04.

// Add one week to the "to" of the other period to avoid overlap.
		// Example: If s is 2021-W01 to 2021-W10 and other is 2021-W01 to 2021-W05.
		// The difference should be 2021-W06 to 2021-W10.

